## Detection Queries

### 1. RDP Brute-Force Detection

**ATT&CK Technique:** T1110.001 — Brute Force: Password Guessing  
**Log Source:** Windows Security Event Log  
**Event ID:** 4625 (Failed logon)

```spl
index=windows sourcetype=WinEventLog:Security EventCode=4625
| stats count by src_ip, user, host
| where count > 10
| sort -count
```

**What it detects:** Source IPs generating more than 10 failed authentication attempts against a host. The threshold of 10 is a starting baseline — in a production environment this would be tuned per subnet and time window.

**True positive indicators:** High count from a single external IP, multiple targeted usernames, attempts outside business hours.

**False positive reduction:** Whitelist known vulnerability scanners, adjust threshold with time-of-day filters, exclude internal monitoring tools.

