### 3. Lateral Movement — Network Logon (Pass the Hash / Remote Access)

**ATT&CK Technique:** T1021 — Remote Services / T1550.002 — Pass the Hash  
**Log Source:** Windows Security Event Log  
**Event ID:** 4624 (Successful logon), Logon Type 3 (Network)

```spl
index=windows sourcetype=WinEventLog:Security EventCode=4624
Logon_Type=3 NOT user="ANONYMOUS LOGON"
| stats count by src_ip, dest_host, user
| where count > 5
| sort -count
```

**What it detects:** Repeated network logons (Type 3) from a single source to multiple hosts — a common pattern in lateral movement, pass-the-hash, and credential spraying.

**Logon types reference:**
| Type | Description |
|------|-------------|
| 2 | Interactive (local console) |
| 3 | Network (SMB, file shares) |
| 10 | Remote interactive (RDP) |

**True positive indicators:** Single src_ip authenticating to 5+ hosts in a short window, NTLM authentication in a Kerberos environment.

