### 5. Data Exfiltration — Large Outbound Transfer

**ATT&CK Technique:** T1048 — Exfiltration Over Alternative Protocol  
**Log Source:** Zeek network logs (`zeek_conn`)

```spl
index=network sourcetype=zeek_conn
| eval mb_sent = bytes_sent / 1048576
| where mb_sent > 50
| stats sum(mb_sent) as total_mb by src_ip, dest_ip
| sort -total_mb
| where total_mb > 200
```

**What it detects:** Internal hosts sending more than 200MB of data to a single external destination — a strong indicator of staged exfiltration.

**Thresholds:** 50MB per session and 200MB aggregate are starting points. Production tuning would baseline normal outbound traffic per host role (e.g. a backup server legitimately transfers large volumes).

**True positive indicators:** Transfer to cloud storage or paste sites, transfer outside business hours, encrypted traffic to an unknown destination, preceded by staging activity (T1074).

